# Clean code
- Named constants instead of magic numbers/strings.
- Names explain purpose; avoid unclear abbreviations.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*; document non-obvious side effects.
- One responsibility per function/file; extract nested conditionals into well-named functions.
- DRY: keep a single source of truth, but don't abstract prematurely.
- Leave code cleaner than you found it; fix small debt while you're there.
- Bug fix → first write a failing test, then fix it.
- Small, focused commits with clear messages. Never force-push.
